id: pm-w16muu
title: CodSpeed instrument cache can stall simulation setup until the hosted benchmark gate is canceled
description: The exact-head CodSpeed workflow restores cached Valgrind instrumentation and then stalls installing /tmp/valgrind-codspeed.deb plus libc6-dbg until the 20-minute job timeout cancels the run before any benchmark starts. Make the free hosted simulation gate deterministic and fail-closed without weakening the benchmark measurement mode.
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[5]: ci,codspeed,github-actions,performance,regression
created_at: "2026-08-19T09:03:37.249Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-19T10:05:44.373Z"
closed_at: "2026-08-19T09:42:05.046Z"
completed_at: "2026-08-19T09:42:05.046Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 60
acceptance_criteria: CodSpeed remains in simulation mode on free GitHub-hosted runners; stale instrument cache reuse cannot hang setup; the workflow contract test prevents regression; an exact-head hosted run completes successfully and uploads benchmarks.
parent: pm-yh6t
risk: medium
confidence: high
severity: high
environment: "GitHub-hosted ubuntu-22.04 image 20260810.260.1, CodSpeedHQ/action v5.0.3, runner 5.0.2, Node 24"
repro_steps: "Run PR #1062 CodSpeed workflow; observe instrument cache hit, package restore, install start, then no benchmark output until timeout cancellation."
resolution: "Pinned CodSpeed to the officially supported ubuntu-22.04 runner family, retained v5.0.3 simulation mode and fresh instrument installation, and strengthened the workflow contract against runner or mode drift."
expected_result: The CodSpeed simulation job reaches and uploads the Vitest benchmark suite within its 20-minute contract on every exact head.
actual_result: "Two consecutive exact-head attempts on ubuntu-22.04 image 20260810.260.1 completed in 2m49s and 2m48s, installed instruments, ran all 11 benchmarks, and uploaded performance data; exact-head CI was fully green."
fixed_version: 2026.8.19
component: ci/codspeed
regression: true
